 "The third one is a plane. A plane is a flat surface that goes on forever, like a floor that never ends. We call these three undefined, because we can only describe them with examples. Everything else in geometry is defined from them.",
 "Now the defined terms, and their symbols. A line gets a symbol with two arrows on top: line A B. Two arrows, because it goes on forever both ways.",
 "A ray has only one arrow. It starts at an endpoint and goes on forever in one direction. Ray A B starts at A, and A is always written first.",
 "A segment has two endpoints, so it has a bar on top, with no arrows. A segment has a beginning and an end, so we can measure it.",
 "When we write A B with no bar at all, it means the length of the segment. That's a number, like five centimeters.",
 "An angle is made of two rays with the same endpoint, called the vertex. We write angle A B C, and the vertex, B, always goes in the middle.",
